{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ec5dac88-0474-4d2a-892f-c3b185ba0f66","agentId":"a732e6a6efcad25ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (mes-log-mcp/server.py is the MES-log MCP server with list_logs/latest_log/search_logs/read_log; mes catalog in mes-log-mcp/mes/catalog.py; CUORE state in CUORE_STATE_DIR (prod C:\\ProgramData\\cuore: observations.jsonl, scans/<vin>/SCAN_*.txt exports, recordings/, owner_events.jsonl, attested, jobs.jsonl)). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no COM3; tests with temp dirs and copies (never modify the prod files). Minimal grepping. Report under 120 words. Others own owner_routes/m_*/labels, fullscan/liveboard/scan_health/scanlog (transmission), system_detail/system.html, dossier_bridge MIL block/analysis clear-assessment: do not edit those; you own mes-log-mcp/server.py (new tools block), mes-log-mcp/mes/catalog.py (additive: a second log root), cuore/api/scanlog.py (additive search endpoint only; re-read first), NEW mes-log-mcp/mes/cuore_log.py, tests under mes-log-mcp/tests/ and cuore/tests/check_cuore_log.py, docs/handbook/02-architecture.md (one additive paragraph). You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/).\n\nOwner's question: \"can we call the CUORE logs just as easily as the MES logs? do we need to improve any log work?\" Build parity:\n1. mes/cuore_log.py: a read-only reader over CUORE_STATE_DIR: list_scans(vin, since, until, kind=full|guided|partial|attempt), latest_scan(vin), read_scan(scan_id) (the full scan dict: codes by status per module, freeze frames every PID, readiness, Mode 06, Mode 09, PIDs, module identities, coverage, bus captures, health verdict line if scan_health is importable), search(pattern, since, until, kinds) regex across observations (all kinds), owner events, attested inputs, hypotheses/jobs audit, recordings' headers — newest first with file/line/context like search_logs; export_scan(scan_id, fmt=json|mes). Reuse cuore.live.scanlog where it exists (import defensively); never duplicate the grouping rule.\n2. MCP tools in mes-log-mcp/server.py (new block): cuore_list_scans, cuore_latest_scan, cuore_read_scan, cuore_search, cuore_export_scan, cuore_log_dir, and a unified `logs_timeline(vin, since, until)` that merges MES logs and CUORE scans into one newest-first list with a \"source\" column (MES scan / MES FES / CUORE full / guided / partial / attempt) so a session can be read end to end.\n3. mes catalog: accept a second root (CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans) so CUORE's MES-format exports appear in list_logs with provenance \"cuore live export\" — exports only, never observations.jsonl itself; make sure the simulation filter and the workup treat them as real (they are from-car) but labelled.\n4. Log hygiene audit (report + implement the safe parts): observations.jsonl growth and rotation (append-only; add a size note and a documented `cuore_log_archive` tool that copies a dated snapshot into CUORE_STATE_DIR/archive/ without truncating; no deletion ever), a per-file sha256 in the archive manifest, and a `cuore_log_integrity` tool that checks every JSONL line parses and reports counts per kind/day. Document all in the handbook paragraph.\nTests: temp state dir with copies of the 2026-10-13 observation lines from C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl: cuore_list_scans returns the real scans with kinds, read_scan has the P0440 freeze frame and Mode 06 3A FAIL, cuore_search \"U1713\" hits the module_dtcs line with context, logs_timeline merges with the MES SCAN_2610080920 entry (copy that file into a temp MES root) in date order with sources, export round-trips through the mes parser, archive creates a snapshot with a manifest and leaves the original untouched, integrity reports counts. Run your tests plus mes-log-mcp's existing tests and check_scanlog.py. Commit \"CUORE log tools: list/latest/read/search/export scans, unified MES+CUORE timeline, archive and integrity, exports visible to the MES catalogue\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report hash."},"uuid":"99ad1a1a-ae09-4b7f-a492-cb11f1d6629b","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:46:23.153Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
