{"parentUuid":"7ef507ed-cbb3-42a6-b10f-2b8d87fa1718","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d6e397a4-8ef0-4e3f-aa12-0e1ab89aceab","agentId":"a732e6a6efcad25ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WkXWtprYzVobMG5pVF4bRb","type":"tool_result","content":"FAIL: tests/check_dashboard.py\n  [ok] empty code_timeline chart root is an <svg>\r\n  [ok] empty odometer chart is well-formed XML\r\n  [ok] empty odometer chart root is an <svg>\r\n  [ok] empty modules chart is well-formed XML\r\n  [ok] empty modules chart root is an <svg>\r\n\r\n1/44 check(s) failed:\r\n  - vehicle name present\npass=29 fail=1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"378031bd-b648-44eb-9294-396f9244fb0c","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:06:18.261Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"FAIL: tests/check_dashboard.py\n  [ok] empty code_timeline chart root is an <svg>\r\n  [ok] empty odometer chart is well-formed XML\r\n  [ok] empty odometer chart root is an <svg>\r\n  [ok] empty modules chart is well-formed XML\r\n  [ok] empty modules chart root is an <svg>\r\n\r\n1/44 check(s) failed:\r\n  - vehicle name present\npass=29 fail=1","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\experience_bridge.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":41,"oldLines":6,"newStart":41,"newLines":29,"lines":[" a ``label`` of \"from <Model> experience: verify fit\" rather than being"," presented as this car's own experience, and (see above) a smaller"," vehicle-fit bonus than an exact-model match.","+","+**Driver/mechanic-added links** (added 2026-10-14, answering the owner's own","+complaint: *\"I need to add Others' experiences input data from driver and","+mechanic ... I am unable to modify these fields\"*) -- :mod:`cuore.live.","+experience_inputs` is the append-only store a \"+ Add what you found\" form","+writes to. :func:`links_for` merges that store's rows for the same","+code/family/job (and ``vin``, when given -- see that module's own docstring","+for exactly how vin-less rows are treated as universal) into the same","+``links`` list the curated table produces, shaped identically plus","+``curated`` (bool), ``found_by`` ``{role, name}``, ``found_at``, ``note``,","+``rating``, ``verified`` ``{status, at, method}``, ``flags`` and","+``worked_count`` -- so one template loop renders both.","+","+Sort order changed with this merge: links are now bucketed by **tier**","+before score -- curated rows (hand-verified by definition, see","+``mes.experience``'s own docstring) are tier 0; a mechanic-added row","+verified reachable is tier 1; a driver-added row verified reachable is tier","+2; everything else (owner/cuore-added, or anything not verified) is tier 3,","+last. Only within a tier does the existing relevance/importance ``score``","+still decide order -- the four ``?exp=`` views on the card re-filter this","+same tiered-then-scored list, so \"relevant\" always means \"curated, then","+mechanic, then driver, then the rest,\" never a plain score sort across","+roles."," \"\"\""," "," from __future__ import annotations"]},{"oldStart":48,"oldLines":6,"newStart":71,"newLines":8,"lines":[" from datetime import date as _date"," from typing import Any, Optional"," ","+from ..live import experience_inputs as _inputs_store","+"," #: relevance points by which lookup found the link, and the reason phrase"," #: that lookup contributes."," _RELEVANCE = {"]},{"oldStart":162,"oldLines":49,"newStart":187,"newLines":201,"lines":["     return scored"," "," ","+#: a user-picked ``kind`` (cuore.live.experience_inputs.KINDS) reuses the","+#: curated table's own importance points via this mapping onto _KIND_SCORE's","+#: keys; anything not listed (article/manual/photo/note) scores like","+#: owner_report.","+_INPUT_KIND_SCORE_KEY = {\"video\": \"how_to_video\", \"forum\": \"forum_thread\", \"audio\": \"sound_reference\"}","+","+#: rating adjustment -- a driver/mechanic's own \"did this help\" signal,","+#: on top of the same importance points a curated row earns.","+_RATING_SCORE = {\"helped\": 5, \"unsure\": 0, \"wrong\": -25}","+","+#: role chip label shown on the card -- curated rows are stamped with the","+#: \"cuore\" role at merge time (see :func:`_curated_as_link`) so one lookup","+#: covers every row.","+ROLE_LABELS = {\"cuore\": \"CUORE curated\", \"mechanic\": \"Mechanic\", \"driver\": \"Driver\", \"owner\": \"Owner\"}","+","+","+def _tier(link: dict[str, Any]) -> int:","+    \"\"\"0 curated, 1 mechanic (verified reachable), 2 driver (verified","+    reachable), 3 everything else (owner/cuore-added, or not verified) --","+    see module docstring for why this bucket comes before ``score``.\"\"\"","+    if link.get(\"curated\"):","+        return 0","+    role = (link.get(\"found_by\") or {}).get(\"role\")","+    verified_ok = (link.get(\"verified\") or {}).get(\"status\") == \"verified\"","+    if not verified_ok:","+        return 3","+    if role == \"mechanic\":","+        return 1","+    if role == \"driver\":","+        return 2","+    return 3","+","+","+def _score_input(view: dict[str, Any], via: str) -> dict[str, Any]:","+    \"\"\"Shape one folded :mod:`cuore.live.experience_inputs` row into the","+    same dict shape a curated link has, with ``score``/``reason`` built","+    from the same relevance+importance signals plus the rating adjustment","+    only a user-added row carries.\"\"\"","+    relevance, relevance_reason = _RELEVANCE[via]","+    reasons = [relevance_reason]","+","+    kind = view.get(\"kind\") or \"note\"","+    kind_key = _INPUT_KIND_SCORE_KEY.get(kind, \"owner_report\")","+    kind_score, kind_reason = _KIND_SCORE.get(kind_key, (5, \"owner report\"))","+    reasons.append(kind_reason)","+","+    verified_ok = (view.get(\"verified\") or {}).get(\"status\") == \"verified\"","+    rep_score = _REPUTATION_SCORE[\"medium\"] if verified_ok else 0","+    if verified_ok:","+        reasons.append(\"verified reachable\")","+","+    rating = view.get(\"rating\") or \"unsure\"","+    rating_score = _RATING_SCORE.get(rating, 0)","+    if rating == \"helped\":","+        reasons.append(\"reported: helped\")","+    elif rating == \"wrong\":","+        reasons.append(\"reported: wrong\")","+","+    recency_score = _recency_score(view.get(\"found_at\"))","+","+    found_by = dict(view.get(\"found_by\") or {})","+    return {","+        \"id\": view.get(\"id\"),","+        \"title\": view.get(\"title\") or view.get(\"url\"),","+        \"url\": view.get(\"url\"),","+        \"source\": _host_of_for_source(view.get(\"url\", \"\")),","+        \"kind\": kind,","+        \"covers\": \"\",","+        \"date\": (view.get(\"found_at\") or \"\")[:10],","+        \"reputation\": \"medium\" if verified_ok else \"\",","+        \"verified_at\": (view.get(\"verified\") or {}).get(\"at\", \"\"),","+        \"verified_how\": (view.get(\"verified\") or {}).get(\"method\", \"\"),","+        \"curated\": False,","+        \"found_by\": found_by,","+        \"found_at\": view.get(\"found_at\"),","+        \"note\": view.get(\"note\", \"\"),","+        \"rating\": rating,","+        \"verified\": view.get(\"verified\") or {},","+        \"score\": relevance + kind_score + rep_score + rating_score + recency_score,","+        \"reason\": \", \".join(reasons),","+    }","+","+","+def _host_of_for_source(url: str) -> str:","+    try:","+        from urllib.parse import urlparse","+        host = (urlparse(url).hostname or \"\").lower()","+        return host[4:] if host.startswith(\"www.\") else host","+    except ValueError:","+        return \"\"","+","+","+def _curated_as_link(scored: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:","+    \"\"\"Stamp a curated (``mes.experience``) row, already scored by","+    :func:`_score_link`, with the fields the merged shape needs: ``curated``","+    True and a ``found_by``/``found_at`` that render through the same","+    \"Found by <role> ... <date>\" chip every row uses.\"\"\"","+    scored = dict(scored)","+    scored[\"curated\"] = True","+    scored[\"found_by\"] = {\"role\": \"cuore\", \"name\": \"CUORE curated\"}","+    scored[\"found_at\"] = scored.get(\"verified_at\") or scored.get(\"date\") or \"\"","+    scored[\"note\"] = scored.get(\"covers\", \"\")","+    scored[\"rating\"] = \"helped\"","+    scored[\"verified\"] = {\"status\": \"verified\" if scored.get(\"verified_at\") else \"unverified\",","+                          \"at\": scored.get(\"verified_at\", \"\"), \"method\": scored.get(\"verified_how\", \"\")}","+    return scored","+","+","+def _attach_feedback(link: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:","+    \"\"\"Best-effort: attach ``flags`` and ``worked_count`` from","+    :mod:`cuore.live.experience_inputs`. Never raises -- a store hiccup just","+    means those two fields come back empty/zero.\"\"\"","+    link = dict(link)","+    lid = str(link.get(\"id\") or \"\")","+    try:","+        link[\"flags\"] = _inputs_store.flags_for(lid) if lid else []","+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001","+        link[\"flags\"] = []","+    try:","+        link[\"worked_count\"] = len(_inputs_store.worked_for(lid)) if lid else 0","+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001","+        link[\"worked_count\"] = 0","+    return link","+","+","+def _matching_inputs(*, code: Optional[str], family: Optional[str], job: Optional[str],","+                     vin: Optional[str]) -> list[tuple[dict[str, Any], str]]:","+    \"\"\"User-added rows (:mod:`cuore.live.experience_inputs`) whose scope","+    matches ``code``/``family``/``job``, each paired with the field that","+    matched (same ``via`` vocabulary the curated lookups use). Best-effort:","+    a store hiccup degrades to no user rows, same posture as everything","+    else in this module.\"\"\"","+    try:","+        rows = _inputs_store.load(vin or \"\")","+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001","+        return []","+    out: list[tuple[dict[str, Any], str]] = []","+    for view in rows:","+        scope = view.get(\"scope\") or {}","+        if code and scope.get(\"code\") == code:","+            out.append((view, \"code\"))","+        elif family and scope.get(\"family\") == family:","+            out.append((view, \"family\"))","+        elif job and scope.get(\"job\") == job:","+            out.append((view, \"job\"))","+    return out","+","+"," def links_for(*, code: Optional[str] = None, family: Optional[str] = None,","-              job: Optional[str] = None, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:","-    \"\"\"Merged, de-duplicated, scored and ordered (highest score first)","-    experience links for whichever of ``code``/``family``/``job`` are","-    given. ``{\"links\": [...], \"count\": n}``, always -- an empty list","-    (never an exception) when ``mes.experience`` is unavailable, nothing","-    was given, or the lookup itself failed. Each link in the result","-    carries a ``score`` (int) and a ``reason`` (str) -- see module","-    docstring for how both are built.","+              job: Optional[str] = None, vin: Optional[str] = None,","+              include_inputs: bool = True) -> dict[str, Any]:","+    \"\"\"Merged, de-duplicated, tiered-then-scored experience links (curated","+    plus driver/mechanic-added -- see module docstring) for whichever of","+    ``code``/``family``/``job`` are given. ``{\"links\": [...], \"count\": n,","+    \"counts\": {role: n}}``, always -- never an exception, even when","+    ``mes.experience`` is unavailable (user-added rows still render) or","+    nothing was given at all (empty list). Each link carries a ``score``","+    (int) and a ``reason`` (str); ``counts`` tallies curated vs. mechanic vs.","+    driver vs. other for the section header (\"12 curated - 3 mechanic\")."," ","     ``vin``, if given, resolves a model via ``mes.platform.model_for_vin``","     and threads ``include_siblings=True`` through so any sourced","     sibling-platform entries (flagged ``sibling_of``/``verify_fit`` by","     ``mes.experience``) are included too, each labeled \"from <Model>","     experience: verify fit\", and scored with the smaller sibling","-    vehicle-fit bonus rather than the exact-model one.","+    vehicle-fit bonus rather than the exact-model one. It also scopes which","+    user-added rows are eligible (plus any vin-less/universal ones -- see","+    :mod:`cuore.live.experience_inputs`).","+","+    Pass ``include_inputs=False`` to get the curated-only legacy behaviour.","     \"\"\"","     experience = _experience_module()","-    if experience is None:","-        return {\"links\": [], \"count\": 0}","-","     model = _model_for_vin(vin)","     include_siblings = bool(model)","     sibling_models = _sibling_model_names(model)"," ","     collected: list[tuple[dict[str, Any], str]] = []","-    try:","-        if code:","-            for link in experience.for_code(code, include_siblings=include_siblings) or []:","-                collected.append((link, \"code\"))","-        if family:","-            for link in experience.for_family(family, include_siblings=include_siblings) or []:","-                collected.append((link, \"family\"))","-        if job:","-            for link in experience.for_job(job, include_siblings=include_siblings) or []:","-                collected.append((link, \"job\"))","-    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a data-module hiccup must never 500 a page","-        return {\"links\": [], \"count\": 0}","+    if experience is not None:","+        try:","+            if code:","+                for link in experience.for_code(code, include_siblings=include_siblings) or []:","+                    collected.append((link, \"code\"))","+            if family:","+                for link in experience.for_family(family, include_siblings=include_siblings) or []:","+                    collected.append((link, \"family\"))","+            if job:","+                for link in experience.for_job(job, include_siblings=include_siblings) or []:","+             