{"parentUuid":"c7be1b8c-96b4-4c8d-b179-2c531834bda4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a732e6a6efcad25ae","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg22ZFob9aoA61V6K9kau","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QCDcNcgoMeLcCMeL1F1bxS","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\02-architecture.md","offset":150,"limit":35},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":231993,"output_tokens":120,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":566},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":120,"cache_read_input_tokens":231993,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":566,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QCDcNcgoMeLcCMeL1F1bxS":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\02-architecture.md","offset":150,"limit":35}},"serverClassifierRequest":"41827c0e-dc4a-42f1-8262-faae15934b99","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg22ZFWjnhyDjUGic1MLL","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a89b287-8e36-428a-9939-e8c6fddfa571","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:10:55.235Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"3a89b287-8e36-428a-9939-e8c6fddfa571","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"a732e6a6efcad25ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCDcNcgoMeLcCMeL1F1bxS","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t`cuore/web/routes.py`'s `_page()` computes `data-marque` once per request from `cuore.services.mes_bridge.marque_for_vin(vin)` (pure passthrough to `mes.platform.marque_for_vin`, confidence-graded VIN-WMI decode: `alfa`/`maserati`/`ferrari`/`unknown`, never guessed) and every `/v/{vin}/*` page inherits it from that one call, instead of each route guessing (previously `data-marque` was hardcoded to `\"alfa\"`).\n151\t\n152\t## MCP tools\n153\t\n154\t### `mes-log-mcp/server.py` (53 tools, via `@mcp.tool`)\n155\t\n156\tCorpus/log: `status`, `list_logs`, `latest_log`, `vehicles`, `read_log`, `search_logs`, `analyze_scan`, `analyze_session`, `get_freeze_frame`, `extract_dtcs`, `dtc_history`, `list_parameters`, `parameter_series`, `module_info`, `failure_type`, `dtc_description`, `log_dir`.\n157\t\n158\tDiagnosis/knowledge: `experience_links`, `actuator_history`, `vehicle_report`, `workup`, `fault_tree`, `diagnosis_verdict` (the evidence gate), `dtc_feel`, `systems_for_code`, `system_correlation`, `part_info`, `electrical_path`, `physical_path`.\n159\t\n160\tRecordings: `list_recordings`, `read_recording`, `recording_series`, `recording_events`, `recording_snapshot`.\n161\t\n162\tAttested records (append-only): `record_dealer_result`/`dealer_results`, `add_note`/`notes`/`edit_note`/`hide_note`, `feedback_list`/`feedback_add`/`feedback_answer`/`feedback_status`, `add_symptom`/`symptoms`/`hide_symptom`, `electrical_inspection_add`/`electrical_inspections`, `job_open`/`job_current`/`job_add_action`/`job_set_hypothesis`.\n163\t\n164\t### `obd2-mcp/server.py` (47 tools, via `@mcp.tool`)\n165\t\n166\tLink/status: `list_ports`, `status`, `mes_state`, `mes_settings`, `connect`, `disconnect`, `set_cable`, `buses`, `modules`, `verify_bus`, `capture`, `audit_log`, `coverage`.\n167\t\n168\tReads (Mode 01-0A, UDS): `read_dtcs`, `read_pending_dtcs`, `read_permanent_dtcs`, `read_pid`, `read_voltage`, `read_supported_pids`, `read_freeze_frame`, `read_vin`, `read_readiness`, `read_module_dtcs`, `read_module_identity`, `read_did`, `scan_modules`, `discover_modules`, `read_mode06`, `read_dtc_detail`, `read_all_module`, `discover_module_dids`.\n169\t\n170\tLearning: `learn_capture`, `learn_correlate`, `learned_dids`, `learn_actuator`, `list_actuators`.\n171\t\n172\tWrites (MCP-only, consent-gated): `run_actuator`, `clear_module_dtcs`, `clear_dtcs`, `send_raw`.\n173\t\n174\tLive session: `live_channels`, `live_session_start`, `live_session_stop`, `live_snapshot`.\n175\t\n176\tMedia: `list_media`, `media_note`.\n177\t\n178\tVerification: `verify_repair`.\n179\t\n180\t## Launchers and keep-alive\n181\t\n182\t- `start-cuore.ps1` -- launches cuore if not already up and opens a page in the default browser (`-Page`, `-Restart`). Only stops a process whose command line is `python -m cuore`, so it never kills an unrelated server.\n183\t- `cuore-keepalive.ps1` -- loop every 10s: starts cuore if nothing listens on `127.0.0.1:5000`, restarts it if `/api/health` fails 3x in a row. Logs to `C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\logs\\server.log` (rotated at 10 MB). Single instance via a named mutex. Run by the scheduled task \"CUORE Server\".\n184\t- `install-cuore-autostart.ps1` -- installs/removes (`-Remove`) that per-user scheduled task (runs `cuore-keepalive.ps1` at logon and every 5 minutes; no admin rights needed)."}]},"uuid":"d6ee8802-577e-4c4f-b95d-9698518dc83b","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:10:55.301Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\02-architecture.md","content":"`cuore/web/routes.py`'s `_page()` computes `data-marque` once per request from `cuore.services.mes_bridge.marque_for_vin(vin)` (pure passthrough to `mes.platform.marque_for_vin`, confidence-graded VIN-WMI decode: `alfa`/`maserati`/`ferrari`/`unknown`, never guessed) and every `/v/{vin}/*` page inherits it from that one call, instead of each route guessing (previously `data-marque` was hardcoded to `\"alfa\"`).\n\n## MCP tools\n\n### `mes-log-mcp/server.py` (53 tools, via `@mcp.tool`)\n\nCorpus/log: `status`, `list_logs`, `latest_log`, `vehicles`, `read_log`, `search_logs`, `analyze_scan`, `analyze_session`, `get_freeze_frame`, `extract_dtcs`, `dtc_history`, `list_parameters`, `parameter_series`, `module_info`, `failure_type`, `dtc_description`, `log_dir`.\n\nDiagnosis/knowledge: `experience_links`, `actuator_history`, `vehicle_report`, `workup`, `fault_tree`, `diagnosis_verdict` (the evidence gate), `dtc_feel`, `systems_for_code`, `system_correlation`, `part_info`, `electrical_path`, `physical_path`.\n\nRecordings: `list_recordings`, `read_recording`, `recording_series`, `recording_events`, `recording_snapshot`.\n\nAttested records (append-only): `record_dealer_result`/`dealer_results`, `add_note`/`notes`/`edit_note`/`hide_note`, `feedback_list`/`feedback_add`/`feedback_answer`/`feedback_status`, `add_symptom`/`symptoms`/`hide_symptom`, `electrical_inspection_add`/`electrical_inspections`, `job_open`/`job_current`/`job_add_action`/`job_set_hypothesis`.\n\n### `obd2-mcp/server.py` (47 tools, via `@mcp.tool`)\n\nLink/status: `list_ports`, `status`, `mes_state`, `mes_settings`, `connect`, `disconnect`, `set_cable`, `buses`, `modules`, `verify_bus`, `capture`, `audit_log`, `coverage`.\n\nReads (Mode 01-0A, UDS): `read_dtcs`, `read_pending_dtcs`, `read_permanent_dtcs`, `read_pid`, `read_voltage`, `read_supported_pids`, `read_freeze_frame`, `read_vin`, `read_readiness`, `read_module_dtcs`, `read_module_identity`, `read_did`, `scan_modules`, `discover_modules`, `read_mode06`, `read_dtc_detail`, `read_all_module`, `discover_module_dids`.\n\nLearning: `learn_capture`, `learn_correlate`, `learned_dids`, `learn_actuator`, `list_actuators`.\n\nWrites (MCP-only, consent-gated): `run_actuator`, `clear_module_dtcs`, `clear_dtcs`, `send_raw`.\n\nLive session: `live_channels`, `live_session_start`, `live_session_stop`, `live_snapshot`.\n\nMedia: `list_media`, `media_note`.\n\nVerification: `verify_repair`.\n\n## Launchers and keep-alive\n\n- `start-cuore.ps1` -- launches cuore if not already up and opens a page in the default browser (`-Page`, `-Restart`). Only stops a process whose command line is `python -m cuore`, so it never kills an unrelated server.\n- `cuore-keepalive.ps1` -- loop every 10s: starts cuore if nothing listens on `127.0.0.1:5000`, restarts it if `/api/health` fails 3x in a row. Logs to `C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\logs\\server.log` (rotated at 10 MB). Single instance via a named mutex. Run by the scheduled task \"CUORE Server\".\n- `install-cuore-autostart.ps1` -- installs/removes (`-Remove`) that per-user scheduled task (runs `cuore-keepalive.ps1` at logon and every 5 minutes; no admin rights needed).","numLines":35,"startLine":150,"totalLines":186}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3a89b287-8e36-428a-9939-e8c6fddfa571","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
