{"parentUuid":"2c0bc394-cc34-42f5-bc5f-358c3ba40b66","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a732e6a6efcad25ae","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg22ZUV61qumXu87hkQME","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pdx5aEh1h5YsMQkQp7eJDp","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\02-architecture.md","old_string":"Attested records (append-only): `record_dealer_result`/`dealer_results`, `add_note`/`notes`/`edit_note`/`hide_note`, `feedback_list`/`feedback_add`/`feedback_answer`/`feedback_status`, `add_symptom`/`symptoms`/`hide_symptom`, `electrical_inspection_add`/`electrical_inspections`, `job_open`/`job_current`/`job_add_action`/`job_set_hypothesis`.\n\n### `obd2-mcp/server.py` (47 tools, via `@mcp.tool`)","new_string":"Attested records (append-only): `record_dealer_result`/`dealer_results`, `add_note`/`notes`/`edit_note`/`hide_note`, `feedback_list`/`feedback_add`/`feedback_answer`/`feedback_status`, `add_symptom`/`symptoms`/`hide_symptom`, `electrical_inspection_add`/`electrical_inspections`, `job_open`/`job_current`/`job_add_action`/`job_set_hypothesis`.\n\nCUORE live-log parity (`mes.cuore_log`, new 2026-10-14): `cuore_list_scans`/`cuore_latest_scan`/`cuore_read_scan`/`cuore_export_scan` read `CUORE_STATE_DIR`'s live-scan log exactly as easily as the MES tools above read MultiEcuScan's -- reusing `cuore.live.scanlog`'s observation-clustering rule (imported defensively; `mes` never duplicates it) rather than re-deriving scans from `observations.jsonl`, and tagging each scan `full`/`guided`/`partial`/`attempt`. `cuore_search` extends `search_logs`'s regex-with-context shape across `observations.jsonl`, `owner_events.jsonl`, `attested.jsonl`, `jobs.jsonl` and recording headers, read directly off disk (not through `cuore.live`, so this still works if that package is not importable). `logs_timeline(vin)` merges the MES and CUORE lists into one newest-first, sourced view. Two things change in `mes.catalog` for this: `LogEntry` now carries a `provenance` field, and a second log root -- `CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/`, where `cuore.live.scanlog.write_mes_export` writes MES-format exports of a live scan on request -- is scanned alongside the configured MES roots and tagged `provenance=\"cuore live export\"`; those exports are real, from-car data (never flagged `simulation`), so `select()`/`workup` include them by default, just labelled differently from a desktop MES scan. `observations.jsonl` itself never enters the MES catalog. Log hygiene: `cuore_log_dir` reports each store file's size; `cuore_log_archive` copies a dated, sha256-manifested snapshot of every CUORE log file into `CUORE_STATE_DIR/archive/` without ever truncating or deleting the originals; `cuore_log_integrity` parses every line of every store and reports counts per kind/op and per day. The same search, independently implemented for its own process, is also reachable over HTTP as `GET /api/scans/search` (`cuore/api/scanlog.py`, additive to the existing `/api/scans/*` routes).\n\n### `obd2-mcp/server.py` (47 tools, via `@mcp.tool`)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1707,"cache_read_input_tokens":232559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1707,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Pdx5aEh1h5YsMQkQp7eJDp":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\02-architecture.md","old_string":"Attested records (append-only): `record_dealer_result`/`dealer_results`, `add_note`/`notes`/`edit_note`/`hide_note`, `feedback_list`/`feedback_add`/`feedback_answer`/`feedback_status`, `add_symptom`/`symptoms`/`hide_symptom`, `electrical_inspection_add`/`electrical_inspections`, `j