configured MES roots and tagged `provenance=\"cuore live export\"`; those exports are real, from-car data (never flagged `simulation`), so `select()`/`workup` include them by default, just labelled differently from a desktop MES scan. `observations.jsonl` itself never enters the MES catalog. Log hygiene: `cuore_log_dir` reports each store file's size; `cuore_log_archive` copies a dated, sha256-manifested snapshot of every CUORE log file into `CUORE_STATE_DIR/archive/` without ever truncating or deleting the originals; `cuore_log_integrity` parses every line of every store and reports counts per kind/op and per day. The same search, independently implemented for its own process, is also reachable over HTTP as `GET /api/scans/search` (`cuore/api/scanlog.py`, additive to the existing `/api/scans/*` routes).\n+\n ### `obd2-mcp/server.py` (47 tools, via `@mcp.tool`)\n \n Link/status: `list_ports`, `status`, `mes_state`, `mes_settings`, `connect`, `disconnect`, `set_cable`, `buses`, `modules`, `verify_bus`, `capture`, `audit_log`, `coverage`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e4697cbd-bf3e-4953-a82e-409fd35a7e05","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e5b23396-47be-4208-b12a-7eed7b2ae88b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
